---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ContactUs from "../../components/astro/ContactUs.astro";
import LogoHoneycomb from "../../components/astro/LogoHoneycomb.astro";
import "../../styles/contract-workflow.css";
const title = "HubSpot Contract Management Setup";
---
<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description="PandaDoc and HubSpot contract workflow setup. Reduce repeated entry, check selected signed details and keep the agreement with the right deal. Free workflow call."
>
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
<header class="header wrap">
  <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="SwotBee home"><LogoHoneycomb width={32} height={30} /><span>SWOT<span class="brand-bee">bee</span></span></a>
  <nav aria-label="Page navigation"><a href="#scope">How we help</a><a href="#process">The process</a><a href="#questions">Questions</a></nav>
  <a class="button button-small" href="#inquiry" data-ga-cta="contract_workflow_request">Discuss your workflow <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
</header>
<main id="main">
  <div class="hero-surface"><section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span>CUSTOMER-CONTRACT IMPLEMENTATION SERVICES</div>
      <h1 id="hero-title">PandaDoc + HubSpot<br /> <span class="highlight">contract workflow</span> setup.</h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">Still re-entering contract details or searching for the signed copy? Get help preparing agreements from deal data, bringing selected signed details back and keeping the completed document with the right HubSpot deal.</p>
      <a class="button" href="#inquiry" data-ga-cta="contract_workflow_request">Request a free workflow call <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <p class="cta-note">Discuss one workflow with Sharmi. Get a short recap of the likely route, dependencies and next step.</p>
      <p class="cta-price-note">Implementation is optional, separately scoped and quoted.</p>
      <p class="other-tools">Using DocuSign or another tool? <a href="#inquiry" data-ga-cta="contract_workflow_request">Tell us what you use.</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="workflow-art" role="img" aria-label="Illustrative workflow: prepare a customer agreement from deal data, complete signing, then review selected fields and the signed PDF on the linked HubSpot deal. This is an example, not a product screenshot.">
      <div class="art-topline"><span class="tiny-dot"></span>ONE AGREEMENT. A CLEAR HANDOFF.<span class="example-label">Example</span></div>
      <div class="document-card">
        <div class="document-head"><div class="document-icon" aria-hidden="true">▤</div><span>CUSTOMER AGREEMENT</span><span class="paper-number">01</span></div>
        <h2>Annual support agreement</h2><p class="doc-sub">Example Services · Support deal</p>
        <div class="document-lines"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
        <div class="document-fields"><div><span>Customer reference</span><strong>CLIENT-101</strong></div><div><span>Term end</span><strong>30 Nov 2027</strong></div></div>
        <div class="signature"><span class="signature-script">Example signature</span><span class="status"><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span> Signed</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="transfer"><span class="transfer-line"></span><span class="transfer-pill"><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span> Selected details + signed PDF</span><span class="transfer-line"></span></div>
      <div class="deal-card"><div class="deal-top"><div class="crm-icon" aria-hidden="true">H</div><div><span class="deal-kicker">HUBSPOT DEAL</span><h3>Example Services / Support</h3></div><span class="deal-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><div class="deal-bottom"><span><span class="check" aria-hidden="true">✓</span> Linked agreement</span><span class="review-badge">Ready for review</span></div></div>
      <div class="art-foot"><span class="shield" aria-hidden="true">◇</span> Check the record. Verify the handoff.</div>
    </div>
  </section>
  </div>
  <section class="principles wrap" aria-label="Service approach"><div><span class="mini-index">01</span><strong>Your existing tools, reviewed first</strong></div><div><span class="mini-index">02</span><strong>One clearly scoped workflow</strong></div><div><span class="mini-index">03</span><strong>A useful next step, before a project</strong></div></section>
  <section class="pain-section" aria-labelledby="pain-title"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">THE MANUAL WORK BETWEEN THE TOOLS</span><h2 id="pain-title">Signed agreements.<br> Manual work still waiting.</h2></div><p>For the people preparing contracts,<br> updating HubSpot and handing work over.</p></div>
    <div class="pain-grid">
      <article><span class="number">01 / PREPARE</span><div class="line-icon" aria-hidden="true">▤<span>↺</span></div><h3>The same details.<br> Entered again.</h3><p>Copying deal details into a template, then checking another spreadsheet before you send it.</p></article>
      <article><span class="number">02 / UPDATE</span><div class="line-icon" aria-hidden="true">⇄</div><h3>The agreement changed.<br> Did HubSpot?</h3><p>Checking signed dates and selected values against the deal, then updating them by hand.</p></article>
      <article><span class="number">03 / HAND OVER</span><div class="line-icon" aria-hidden="true">⌕</div><h3>One customer.<br> Which agreement?</h3><p>Finding the signed copy and working out which deal and person should receive it before handover or renewal review.</p></article>
    </div>
    <div class="section-afterword">Tell us where the handoff breaks. We’ll look at one workflow with you before proposing changes.<a href="#inquiry" data-ga-cta="contract_workflow_request">Let’s discuss it <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  </div></section>
  <section id="scope" class="scope-section wrap" aria-labelledby="scope-title">
    <div class="scope-intro"><span class="eyebrow">WHAT A SCOPED IMPLEMENTATION CAN COVER</span><h2 id="scope-title">A workflow your team<br> can use and check.</h2><p>Agree what we configure, how we check it and what your team receives. We review your existing tools before proposing custom work.</p><div class="scope-note"><span aria-hidden="true">↳</span><p>Existing native configuration may be sufficient. We’ll start there.</p></div></div>
    <div class="scope-list"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Prepare from the intended deal</h3><p>Configure an agreed template and supported fields around the deal information your team already maintains.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Check the signed-document handoff</h3><p>Agree which values and completed PDF should reach which record, then verify the supported route against agreed test cases.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Give the operator a usable handover</h3><p>Document the agreed setup, routine checks, the responsible person and what to do when a handoff needs attention.</p></div></article><p class="scope-qualifier">Your quote confirms the deliverables and checks. Scope depends on your tools, subscriptions, templates and business rules.</p></div>
  </section>
  <section class="example-section wrap" aria-labelledby="example-title"><div class="example-panel"><div><span class="eyebrow">A WORKED EXAMPLE</span><h2 id="example-title">One customer.<br> Two deals.<br> The right agreement.</h2><p>A support agreement starts from the intended deal. After signing, selected details and the completed PDF belong with that record. The separate project agreement stays with its own deal.</p><ul class="example-checks" aria-label="Example acceptance checks"><li>Confirm the intended deal and document.</li><li>Compare the agreed fields with the signed source.</li><li>Give the responsible person a clear next check.</li></ul></div><div class="example-map"><div class="customer-node"><span class="node-icon" aria-hidden="true">E</span><div><small>CUSTOMER</small><strong>Example Services</strong></div></div><div class="map-branch" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="map-deals"><div class="map-deal selected"><span class="map-label">Support deal</span><strong>Annual agreement</strong><span class="map-tag"><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span> Linked document</span></div><div class="map-deal"><span class="map-label">Separate project</span><strong>Project agreement</strong><span class="map-muted">Separate record</span></div></div><p>Illustrative workflow, not a customer result.<br> Your tools and agreed scope determine the actual setup.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="wrap worked-guide" aria-labelledby="worked-guide-title">
    <h2 id="worked-guide-title">Explore a native-record worked example</h2>
    <p><a href="/posts/hubspot-contracts-renewal-quotes/">Watch the Contract draft check and handoff guide</a>, with a freely usable workbook and workflow PDF. It shows a fictional proposal and a prepared native HubSpot Contract draft. It does not demonstrate a tested PandaDoc signing integration, signed-field writeback or live billing.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="process" class="process-section wrap" aria-labelledby="process-title"><div class="center-heading"><span class="eyebrow">A SMALL FIRST STEP</span><h2 id="process-title">Start with a conversation.<br> Leave with a useful next step.</h2></div><div class="process-grid"><article><span class="step-circle">1</span><h3>Show us where work repeats</h3><p>Tell Sharmi which tools you use, what you do manually and what you want to change.</p></article><article><span class="step-circle">2</span><h3>Get your workflow recap</h3><p>Receive a short summary of the likely route, important dependencies and the next step to consider.</p></article><article><span class="step-circle">3</span><h3>Decide on a scoped project</h3><p>If implementation fits, review separate deliverables, costs, dependencies and checks before deciding to proceed.</p></article></div><p class="process-footnote">Free initial conversation. No contract uploads or account credentials needed.</p></section>
  <section id="questions" class="faq-section wrap" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><div><span class="eyebrow">A FEW THINGS TO KNOW</span><h2 id="faq-title">Before we talk.</h2><p>A clear scope starts with<br> clear expectations.</p></div><div class="faq-list">
    <details open><summary>Is this software or an implementation service?<span aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><p>This is an implementation service. We assess your existing workflow and propose the appropriate configuration or integration work.</p></details>
    <details><summary>We already have an integration. Can you still help?<span aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><p>Yes. Describe what works and what still requires manual work. We first assess whether your existing configuration can meet the need.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Will our current HubSpot and signing-tool plans support this?<span aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><p>It depends on the workflow and features you need. Tell us which tools and plans you use. We identify the important dependencies and assess the supported route before quoting. Some workflows may require additional vendor features or licenses.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Do we have to change signing tools?<span aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><p>A change is not assumed. Tell us your current tools and constraints. The PandaDoc example does not establish identical functionality in another tool.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What does implementation cost?<span aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><p>We quote after understanding the workflow, tools and dependencies. Your quote separates implementation from any additional vendor licenses or recurring tool costs, and states the agreed deliverables and checks.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can we discuss renewals or mid-term changes?<span aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><p>Yes. Tell us whether the difficulty is preparing agreements, keeping signed details with the right record, or managing dates and ownership for renewal. Renewal tracking, amendments, migration and billing are assessed as separate scopes.</p></details>
  </div></section>
  <section id="inquiry" class="inquiry-section" aria-labelledby="inquiry-title"><div class="wrap inquiry-grid"><div class="inquiry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">LET’S LOOK AT YOUR WORKFLOW</span><h2 id="inquiry-title">What would you<br> like to stop<br> <span>doing manually?</span></h2><p>Tell us where the contract work gets stuck, whether you are setting up a new process or improving an existing integration.</p><div class="person"><div class="person-avatar" aria-hidden="true">S</div><div><strong>You’ll speak with Sharmi</strong><span>Discovery, scoping and implementation</span></div></div><div class="offer-note"><strong>Free workflow call + short recap</strong><p>Discuss one workflow and receive the likely route, dependencies and next step. Implementation is optional, separately scoped and quoted.</p></div></div>
    <div class="form-card inquiry-form"><h3>Request a free workflow call</h3><p class="form-intro">A sentence about your current process is enough.</p><ContactUs variant="contract-workflow" preview={false} /><p class="form-intro">Prefer email? <a href="mailto:info@swotbee.com">Contact info@swotbee.com</a>.</p></div>
  </div></section>
</main>
<footer class="footer wrap"><a class="brand" href="#main" aria-label="SwotBee, back to top"><LogoHoneycomb width={32} height={30} /><span>SWOT<span class="brand-bee">bee</span></span></a><p>Independent implementation services.<br> HubSpot and PandaDoc are third-party platforms.</p><span class="footer-review"><a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> · <a href="/terms/">Terms</a> · <a href="/contactus/">Contact</a><br /><button type="button" data-consent-reopen>Cookie settings</button></span></footer>

</BaseLayout>
